WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.963
An earlier test: 504.5 million word-sized pieces of text,

2
00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:08.469
sealed into separate parts.

3
00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:11.561
It ran on a cloud machine

4
00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:13.268
that has since been shut down.

5
00:00:13.268 --> 00:00:14.997
These are our own records.

6
00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:18.301
A full exact search over

7
00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:20.522
it matched the known-correct answer.

8
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.524
Then we switched one part off.

9
00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:27.990
It still answered most searches, with no wrong passages.

10
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.230
It was not fast.

11
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.905
Building an index on the same machine:

12
00:00:35.905 --> 00:00:38.429
the memory used while building dropped

13
00:00:38.429 --> 00:00:40.606
by 62 percent in a later run.

14
00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:44.329
One run each, with different settings,

15
00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:46.827
so it is not a like-for-like comparison.

16
00:00:46.827 --> 00:00:49.326
This is about building, not serving.

17
00:00:52.976 --> 00:00:55.742
Now the sealed library we search through TRACE.

18
00:00:55.992 --> 00:00:59.720
Searching a huge library normally means reading all of it.

19
00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.908
The library sorts itself into groups.

20
00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.380
A question opens only the likely ones.

21
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.928
The rest is not scored for this search.

22
00:01:17.678 --> 00:01:19.291
A real recorded search:

23
00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:22.066
the same top results as a full scan.

24
00:01:23.978 --> 00:01:26.276
Each comes with a record you can check.

25
00:01:31.578 --> 00:01:35.280
On our test searches, on one of four equal parts:

26
00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.849
about 127 times less scoring work,

27
00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:41.122
and nearly all of the exact answer kept.

28
00:01:46.972 --> 00:01:47.990
The honest part:

29
00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:51.364
at this size a plain scan takes less time per search,

30
00:01:51.364 --> 00:01:53.147
our index is bigger on disk,

31
00:01:53.147 --> 00:01:56.389
and keyword search found the source more often.

32
00:02:01.339 --> 00:02:04.282
We have not built TRACE past that earlier test.

33
00:02:04.282 --> 00:02:05.972
Our saving is scoring work;

34
00:02:05.972 --> 00:02:08.414
where it pays off is not shown yet.

35
00:02:13.364 --> 00:02:16.430
Try the explorer. Running it yourself is planned.

